{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass.</b> He began to say, 'with a strong hand He brought us out,' and returned to explain what the strong hand was — namely, the plague of the firstborn, for through this they went out from Egypt, and not through the earlier plagues. So too the psalmist said: 'To Him who struck Egypt through their firstborn, for His kindness is forever' (Psalms 136:10). And Moses took a short route, for it was already known from his saying 'and YHWH killed every firstborn' that He saved our firstborn and the firstborn of our animals. And with this he connects 'therefore I sacrifice,' and not with the killing of the firstborn:" "<b>Every firstborn of males.</b> Of the species fit for sacrifice before HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:10.683626529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}